{"duration_api_ms":429228,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"ada61010-1feb-459c-a58a-1fa5d8d8abb1","total_cost_usd":2.663674800000001,"usage":{"input_tokens":6,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1338,"cache_read_input_tokens":198618,"output_tokens":1484,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":66},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1338,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1246,"cache_read_input_tokens":99595,"cache_creation_input_tokens":766,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":766},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":58,"outputTokens":18758,"cacheReadInputTokens":2086394,"cacheCreationInputTokens":66872,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":1.3220548,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":3724,"cacheCreationEphemeral5mInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationEphemeral1hInputTokens":65008,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"},"claude-fable-5-1":{"inputTokens":73287,"outputTokens":12175,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":1.34162,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"thinkingTokens":0,"cacheCreationEphemeral5mInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationEphemeral1hInputTokens":0,"canonicalModel":"claude-fable-5-1","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","origin":{"kind":"task-notification","producer":"session-task","runId":"0mw0zn7nl-29a3e76b"},"subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"safety_stops":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":2,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"I finished PKT-0108. The finding: none of the in-process options I tried saves 0.2 s or more, so P3 should not build an in-process cut. The remaining lever is a converter process that stays alive between conversions. All three acceptance commands pass (`test -s`, `theseus validate` with 0 errors, `x2t.sh` with both the direct and browser parts passing), `theseus scope-check` is clean, and the work is committed as 83acf53.\n\n**Where the time goes** (empty documents → PDF, snapshots on):\n- **Fixed part:** about 60 ms to start the process and about 145 ms to load the snapshot.\n- **Per-document JavaScript:** for docx, opening the file data takes 250–300 ms; for pptx, laying out the document takes about 455 ms.\n- **CPU profile:** about 70% is real JavaScript work (font tables, default styles, reading the file, layout), about 20% is V8's own time (compiler and native code, compilation at most part of it) and 4–13% is garbage collection. So the time is mostly real work, not compiling code a snapshot could keep.\n\n**Options tried** (median of 5, wall time and CPU time; xlsx was timed but not profiled):\n- **V8 flags** (`--single-threaded`, `--no-opt`, `--no-lazy-feedback-allocation`): at most about 0.05–0.08 s, which is within run-to-run noise.\n- **`--max-lazy`:** crashes docx → pdf.\n- **Snapshot made with compilation forced up front (`--no-lazy`):** 0.12–0.17 s slower, because the snapshot files are about 2.2 times larger and take longer to load.\n- **Output equality:** the forced-compilation snapshot and the `--no-lazy-feedback-allocation` setting produce output equal to the baseline on the corpus.\n\n**What I decided:**\n- **No core changes:** the packet lists no target files in `external/core`, so I didn't change or build it. V8 flags are passed to the installed x2t through a small preloaded library (`x2t-v8flags-shim.c`), which works because `libdoctrenderer.so` exports `v8::V8::SetFlagsFromString`.\n- **Real \"after warm-up\" snapshot:** not built. It would need the snapshot code to provide the native objects, a large C++ change. I sized it in the note instead: at most about 0.1 s, which is below the threshold.\n- **Separate test copies:** every option ran in its own copy of the converter in the scratch directory, so the live server was never touched.\n- **CPU time as well as wall time:** other sessions kept the 2-CPU VM busy (load 3.3–4.7), and wall-clock medians moved by up to 60% between runs. The timing script therefore also records CPU time.\n\n**Files added:**\n- `.theseus/diagnosis/PKT-x2t-r2-warmup.md`: the time split, option table, equality results and P3 verdict.\n- `.theseus/oracle/perf/x2t-warmup.sh`, `x2t-warmup-time.py` and `x2t-v8flags-shim.c`: the scripts to rerun it.\n- The Executor log, the Lessons for the Atlas and my friction line.\n\n**Lessons for the Atlas:**\n- V8 flags can be tested on x2t without rebuilding core, through that preloaded library.\n- The warm-up is per-document JavaScript work. V8 settings recover less than 0.1 s; only a converter that stays alive removes it.\n- On this VM, record CPU time next to wall time.","ttft_ms":3931,"type":"result","duration_ms":18326,"uuid":"2dfe2d9b-4c9e-4c63-b8f8-25f270f6dfc8","ttft_stream_ms":1739,"time_to_request_ms":73,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":3,"system_prompt":3,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":3,"input_attachments":8,"input_hooks":2,"conversation_append":2,"transcript_persist":1,"tool_pool_refresh":0,"init_message":5,"init_frame_send":1,"engine_pickup":3,"loop_entry":9,"message_prep":1,"model_config_wait":1,"autocompact":2,"request_announcements":4,"query_setup":2,"auto_mode_context_wait":1,"model_gates":0,"tool_schema_build":5,"message_normalization":8,"client_creation":2,"request_build":7},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":1,"time_to_request_loop_